# The tree lab, interactive: the shared editor chrome of the 3D examples (LabEditor: the camera bar
# with orbit and the free WASD camera, the "..." menu, the debug readout, the side panel with the
# shared sky, time of day and date, shadows and TAA) and in its side panel the scenes (LabScenes:
# Forest, the default; One tree; Reference T02; Studies) and the Reference scene's fixed framings as
# camera buttons. A scene is built the first time it is picked and kept. A scripted run (headless,
# a screenshot or the dolly) has no editor and starts as below, so its pictures do not change;
# RAE_TREELAB_EDITOR=1 keeps the editor in one (a picture of the panel; RAE_SETTINGS_OPEN=1 opens
# it).
#
# The tree lab (docs/reference-tree-plan.md step 1): the scene the new tree
# generator is built and judged in, against ONE reference tree, crop T02 of
# the private reference study. The tree is lib/treeGen's (LabTree.rae); the
# background trees, bushes and clouds are placeholders of cylinders and
# spheres. Built new: it uses no older tree code of the lib (the plan's
# "Built new" list), only lib/treeGen, the renderer, the lib GPU grass and
# plain meshes.
#
# The tree is lib/treeGen's (step 3 on: the bare wood so far), seed
# RAE_TREELAB_SEED (default 1); RAE_TREELAB_TREE=levels draws it as a forest
# kind (near, middle and impostor levels, RAE_TREE_LEVEL to pin one:
# reference-tree step 7); RAE_TREELAB_TREE=placeholder shows step 1's
# cylinder and spheres instead.
#
# Cameras (RAE_TREELAB_CAMERA):
#   near (default)  T02's own framing of the 12.5 m tree: from eye height
#                   15.2 m away, looking 18 degrees up, the trunk's foot
#                   near the bottom edge, the top near the top edge
#   mid             the same tree from 40 m
#   far             the same tree from 120 m
#   bark            the trunk up close (4 m), for its color and streaks
#   row             the traced tree and three trees grown from its measures
#                   (treeGen/TreeGrower) beside it, from 32 m (also
#                   RAE_TREELAB_ROW=1 with another camera)
#   fork            the first grown tree's fork and branch joints up close
#                   (6 m, looking up), with the row
#   tracedFork      the same view of the traced tree
#   small           a 6 m tree (RAE_TREELAB_SPECIES) from 13 m at eye height
#   bush            the bush (RAE_TREELAB_SPECIES=15, scale 1) from 3 m
#
# The studies (LabStudies.rae): RAE_TREELAB_STUDY=<view> shows one of the
# meadow flower study scenes that Autumn Grove (138) held before it became
# the low-poly museum (flowers, bellflowers and its two other views) in
# place of the T02 scene.
#
# The forest scene (LabForest.rae): RAE_TREELAB_SCENE=forest shows a tree
# set as a forest at every distance, RAE_TREE_SET=lowPoly|stylized picks
# which (stylized when unset), the T key switches between the two;
# RAE_TREELAB_CAMERA=high looks from 35 m.
#
# The seasons' date and place (LabSeason.rae): RAE_DAY_OF_YEAR,
# RAE_LATITUDE and RAE_YEAR_SPEED set them, and a day slider along the
# bottom shows the date, the latitude and the nearest city (drag it, or
# hold , and .; Y hides it; hidden in headless and screenshot runs).
#
# RAE_TREELAB_DOLLY=<folder>: the camera moves from 20 m to 170 m away from
# the tree over labDollyFrames frames, each saved as a picture in the folder
# (frame0.bmp ...), then the lab ends: the camera move that shows whether
# the levels' switches are seen (with RAE_TREELAB_TREE=levels).
#
# The comparison picture (T02 beside the render, same height):
#   examples/146_treeLab/compare.sh [near|mid|far]
# The scene look (LabLook: haze, warm sun and cool shade, grade, glow) is on;
# RAE_TREELAB_LOOK=plain keeps the renderer's defaults for a before/after.
# A plain screenshot:
#   RAE_SDL_HEADLESS_MS=4000 RAE_GPU2D_SCREENSHOT=/tmp/lab.bmp \
#     rae run examples/146_treeLab/Main.rae
